# The signers whose evidence this host's integrator accepts, one verifier
# key per line in `attest key` format: the name a key signs under, the note
# format's four-byte key hash over that name and key, and base64 of the
# algorithm byte and the raw ed25519 public key. Public keys only — nothing
# here is a secret, which is why it is a plain file in this repo rather
# than an agenix secret.
#
# This file is the identity registry's INTERIM COMPILATION. Identity is a
# governed registry (the-valley .the-valley/decisions/dcr-b87f6e8): entries
# are declared there and compiled into what each enforcement boundary
# checks. No compiler exists yet, so the compiled artifact is written out
# by hand here, and this file is deleted the day the registry compiles.
# Nothing may start parsing a registry before then.
#
# Every key below is already published in secrets/keys.nix; the lines are
# the same ed25519 public keys re-encoded into the format attest reads. A
# key hash binds the NAME to the key, so a key published under a second
# name is a second, unrelated verifier key — the names here are the ones
# `attest` signs under by default (the machine's hostname + /attestations).
#
# Evidence signed by nobody in this file does not transfer. That is
# reported per check, not treated as a forgery.

